{"step_index":282,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T16:41:44Z","thinking":"Encoding must be Windows-1251 for the Lua file. Will create `Y:\\SIGNAL\\tick_parser.lua` based on the user's examples, prioritizing a parser similar to the reader and writer modules.\n\n\nThe Lua code's structure and variable naming conventions will follow specified rules, particularly snake_case for time-related variables and dot notation for table access. The `ParseTicks` function will be defined with the input file, output directory, and period time as parameters and will handle file operations. The code will write to `candles.txt`, `high_prices.txt`, `low_prices.txt`, and `close_prices.txt` in the specified output directory, following the defined format.\n\n\nThe Lua code opens output files for candles, high prices, low prices, and close prices, checking for successful file creation. It initializes variables to store the current candle's data: date, time, open, high, low, close, and volume. A `FlushBar` function is defined to write the candle data to files, formatting the output string with date, time, and price values.\n\n\nProcessing each line of the input file involves skipping blank lines and the header, then extracting data fields (ticker, period, date, time, price, volume) using a regular expression match. Numerical values for price and volume are extracted, ensuring the time string has sufficient length for processing hours, minutes, and seconds. Time is calculated in seconds, then mapped to a time slot index based on the specified period.\n\nIf a new time slot is detected, the current bar data is flushed to output files using the `FlushBar` function. Subsequently, the current time slot, date, and time are updated, and the open, high, low, close and volume are initialized with the current price and volume. If the time slot remains the same, the code will continue to update the high, low, and close prices if necessary.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"& \"Y:\\SIGNAL\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\" -c \"\nimport lupa, time\n\nlua = lupa.LuaRuntime()\nlua_code = '''\nfunction ParseTicks(input_file, output_dir, period_time)\n    if not input_file then return nil, 'No input file' end\n    output_dir = output_dir or 'Y:\\\\\\\\SIGNAL'\n    period_time = period_time or 300\n\n    local candles_file = output_dir .. '\\\\\\\\candles.txt'\n    local high_file    = output_dir .. '\\\\\\\\high_prices.txt'\n    local low_file     = output_dir .. '\\\\\\\\low_prices.txt'\n    local close_file   = output_dir .. '\\\\\\\\close_prices.txt'\n\n    local f_candles = io.open(candles_file, 'w')\n    local f_high    = io.open(high_file, 'w')\n    local f_low     = io.open(low_file, 'w')\n    local f_close   = io.open(close_file, 'w')\n\n    if not f_candles or not f_high or not f_low or not f_close then\n        return nil, 'Cannot open output files'\n    end\n\n    local candles = {}\n    local current_slot = -1\n    local current_date = ''\n    local current_time = ''\n\n    local cur_open = 0\n    local cur_high = 0\n    local cur_low  = 0\n    local cur_close = 0\n    local cur_vol  = 0\n\n    local function FlushBar()\n        if current_slot < 0 then return end\n\n        f_candles:write(string.format('%s;%s;%.1f;%.1f;%.1f;%.1f;%d\\\\n',\n            current_date, current_time, cur_open, cur_high, cur_low, cur_close, cur_vol))\n\n        f_high:write(string.format('%s;%s;%.1f\\\\n', current_date, current_time, cur_high))\n        f_low:write(string.format('%s;%s;%.1f\\\\n', current_date, current_time, cur_low))\n        f_close:write(string.format('%s;%s;%.1f\\\\n', current_date, current_time, cur_close))\n\n        local c = {}\n        c.date = current_date\n        c.time = current_time\n        c.open = cur_open\n        c.high = cur_high\n        c.low = cur_low\n        c.close = cur_close\n        c.volume = cur_vol\n        table.insert(candles, c)\n    end\n\n    for line in io.lines(input_file) do\n        if line and line ~= '' and not line:find('<TICKER>') then\n            local ticker, per, d, t, p_str, v_str = line:match('^([^,]+),([^,]+),([^,]+),([^,]+),([^,]+),([^,]+)')\n            if ticker and t and p_str then\n                local price = tonumber(p_str)\n                local vol   = tonumber(v_str) or 1\n\n                if price and #t >= 6 then\n                    local h = tonumber(t:sub(1, 2)) or 0\n                    local m = tonumber(t:sub(3, 4)) or 0\n                    local s = tonumber(t:sub(5, 6)) or 0\n                    local sec_total = h * 3600 + m * 60 + s\n                    local slot_idx = math.floor(sec_total / period_time)\n\n                    if slot_idx ~= current_slot then\n                        FlushBar()\n\n                        current_slot = slot_idx\n                        current_date = d\n\n                        local slot_sec = slot_idx * period_time\n                        local bar_h = math.floor(slot_sec / 3600)\n                        local bar_m = math.floor((slot_sec % 3600) / 60)\n                        current_time = string.format('%02d:%02d:00', bar_h, bar_m)\n\n                        cur_open = price\n                        cur_high = price\n                        cur_low  = price\n                        cur_close = price\n                        cur_vol  = vol\n                    else\n                        if price > cur_high then cur_high = price end\n                        if price < cur_low  then cur_low  = price end\n                        cur_close = price\n                        cur_vol = cur_vol + vol\n                    end\n                end\n            end\n        end\n    end\n\n    FlushBar()\n\n    f_candles:close()\n    f_high:close()\n    f_low:close()\n    f_close:close()\n\n    return candles\nend\n'''\nlua.execute(lua_code)\nt0 = time.time()\ncandles = lua.globals().ParseTicks('Y:/MXU6_260907_260907.txt', 'Y:/SIGNAL', 300)\nt1 = time.time()\nprint(f'Done in {t1-t0:.3f} sec. Generated {len(candles)} M5 candles!')\n\"","Cwd":"Y:\\SIGNAL","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing ParseTicks on MXU6_260907","toolSummary":"Test ParseTicks in Lua"}}]}
