не парсят). Я дожен был залить. Если не залито, делай как знаешь. Максимально в моем стиле чтоб я читать мог\n9. Да. И лупу покажи да расскажи\n10. @[Quote] 100% русские делали. Вижу русский след в названии. Другие бы LuPy назвали)\n\n\"Y:/MXU6_260907_260907.txt\" адрес-то должен быть ...динамический. Как сказать? ПРограмма должна читать файл лежащий в ее папке. Либо нужен выбор файла в меню программы.\n\nЯ положил что мы будем читать. Там свежее\n\nДавай\n\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Goal:** Develop a Python + Lua analytical visualization program named **SIGNAL** located at `Y:\\SIGNAL\\`.\n- **Functionality:** Reads Finam tick/candle files, executes a Lua script to calculate M5 candles, EMA(12/26), MACD divergence, regression trends with deviation, and regression along MACD divergence (\"волны/холмы гистограммы\"). Displays candles on the top plot and MACD on the bottom synchronized plot.\n- **Role/Persona Constraints:**\n  - Female persona (\"поняла\", \"сделала\", \"написала\"), friendly, mentor/teacher role (\"на ты\"), gentle explanations of trading/coding concepts, ignore Russian typos completely.\n  - **Crucial Rule:** Do NOT write large unsolicited code dumps (\"Ты сама не пиши пока не попрошу. Ты меня учи\"). Explain architecture, terms, and mechanics step by step.\n  - Lua standards: Windows-1251 (CP1251), no Unicode emojis, dot-notation table assignments, `snake_case` for time variables, external files named in 2 words `snake_case`.\n  - Python standards: Dedicated `.venv`, launcher `.bat` with relative path `\".venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\" \"main.py\"`, `.gitignore`.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Stage 1 (Completed & Verified):**\n  - `Y:\\SIGNAL\\chart_canvas.py`: Two-panel canvas (`pg.GraphicsLayoutWidget`) with top plot for candles (70%) and bottom for MACD (30%), synchronized X-axis (`setXLink`), fixed axis widths (`70px`), dark theme (`#111111`), and dashed zero line.\n  - `Y:\\SIGNAL\\main.py`: Entry point using `QApplication` and `QMainWindow`.\n  - `Y:\\SIGNAL\\.venv`: Dedicated virtual environment with `PyQt6`, `pyqtgraph`, `lupa`, `pandas`, `numpy`.\n  - `Y:\\SIGNAL\\run_signal.bat`: Portable batch launcher with relative path and error pausing.\n  - `Y:\\SIGNAL\\.gitignore`: Excludes `.venv/` and python cache.\n  - Tested: User ran `run_signal.bat` and confirmed the 2-panel window opens and works properly.\n- **Roadmap & System Docs (`TODO_SIGNAL.md`):**\n  - Updated with: triple-splitter system (horizontal between charts, vertical for right menu, range slider for candle count), ghost mode / dimming (alpha=0.2 for candles outside focus), focus interval (3..all candles), EMA overlay, visibility toggles (\"лампочки\"), and `settings.json` persistence.\n- **Stage 2 (Completed):**\n  - `Y:\\SIGNAL\\tick_parser.lua`: CP1251 Lua script implementing `ParseTicks(input_file, output_dir, period_time)`. Parses Finam tick files (`<TICKER>,<PER>,<DATE>,<TIME>,<LAST>,<VOL>`), aggregates into 5-minute M5 candles in 0.24 seconds (for ~90k ticks), and generates 4 files with date and exact candle time (`date;time;...`):\n    1. `candles.txt`: `date;time;open;high;low;close;volume`\n    2. `high_prices.txt`: `date;time;high`\n    3. `low_prices.txt`: `date;time;low`\n    4. `close_prices.txt`: `date;time;close`\n    Also returns the table of candles directly in memory for Python via `lupa`.\n- **Git Repositories:**\n  - `PanicCTRL/boltalka.git`: Synced with dialogue transcripts, `SIGNAL/`, `split_fractal/`, and Antigravity brain backups.\n  - `PanicCTRL/AGENTS.git` (branch `split_fractals`): Updated `AGENTS.md` (and global `~/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md`) with the new rule requiring dedicated `.venv` and relative `.bat` for all Python projects.\n  - `PanicCTRL/SIGNAL.git`: Remote designated by user for pushing SIGNAL after successful candle rendering.\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- **Data & Speed:** Parsing 90,767 ticks into 203 M5 bars in Lua via `lupa` took only 0.24s.\n- **File Structure:** User wants files saved to disk for robot startup caching in addition to memory return for Python.\n- **Rendering Performance:** In `pyqtgraph`, all wicks must be batched into a single `PlotCurveItem` and bodies into `BarGraphItem` (green `#26a69a`, red `#ef5350`) to maintain 60 FPS.\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- The user just stated:\n  1. *\"LuPa («Лупа») 100% русские делали...\"*\n  2. The input file path must be dynamic: auto-detect tick files in the project folder or provide a file chooser menu/dialog (`QFileDialog`).\n  3. The user uploaded/placed a fresh file to read (need to check `Y:\\SIGNAL` or `Y:\\` for newly added `.txt` files).\n  4. User said *\"Давай\"* — ready to see how `plot_candles` is implemented and how `lupa` bridges the data to the chart.\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **Detect New File:** Check `Y:\\SIGNAL` and `Y:\\` for the fresh file the user just placed.\n2. **Implement Dynamic File Path:** In `main.py` / `data_loader.py`, support scanning the folder for default `*.txt` or opening via `QFileDialog`.\n3. **Teach & Add `plot_candles`:**\n   - Explain and add the `plot_candles(df_candles)` method to `chart_canvas.py` using batched wicks (`PlotCurveItem`) and bodies (`BarGraphItem`).\n4. **Integrate `lupa` in `main.py`:**\n   - Call `tick_parser.lua` via `lupa`, get candles, and pass them to `canvas.plot_candles(...)`.\n5. **Run & Test:** Launch via `run_signal.bat`, confirm candles render on the top chart.\n6. **Push to GitHub:** Initialize and push the working codebase to `https://github.com/PanicCTRL/SIGNAL.git`.\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Explain line by line what each block does before/while applying changes.\n- Push to `https://github.com/PanicCTRL/SIGNAL.git` once the candle rendering is successfully running.\n- Maintain the user's specific formatting preferences (semicolons, date and candle time included in all price exports).\n</summary>"}
