{"step_index":319,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T17:01:25Z","thinking":"Considering candlestick rendering and time axis design, a `TimeAxisItem` will override `tickStrings`. This function will utilize a pre-stored list of time strings that correspond to integer indices to provide formatted time labels.\n\n\nThe `TimeAxisItem` is correctly integrated, ensuring time labels are aligned with the plots. Candle rendering relies on a list of tuples containing open, close, low, and high values for each candlestick. Colors are defined for bullish and bearish candles, along with a body width.\n\nThe logic for drawing the candlestick includes a check for doji (open == close) to draw a thin line instead of a full rectangle body. Confirmed that the `generatePicture()` function correctly handles these rendering rules.\n\n\nInitialization sets up the data storage and pre-renders the candlestick plot with an empty picture; data updates trigger re-generation. The candlestick generation loop iterates through provided data points, setting colors based on open/close values and drawing wick an